    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44044" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēvĭrālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		sevir, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a sexvir</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ludi,</span>”
				<i>of the equestrian sexvirs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. M. Aurel. 6</span></i>
			: cena, <i>of the Augustan
			sexvirs.</i>—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēvĭrā-les</span></b> ,
			ium, <i>the Augustan sexvirs</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ORDO SEVIRALIVM,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2229</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 1104, 7</span></i>.</div>
